From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 23:40:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: remove surviving Zed-cloud egress + sign-in surface
 from client

The admin-impersonation path was a live cloud egress that outlived the
cloud strip. In authenticate_with_browser, when ZED_IMPERSONATE and
ZED_ADMIN_API_TOKEN were both set, the client POSTed to
cloud.zed.dev/internal/users/impersonate via authenticate_as_admin. It
slipped through because the verify gate's build_zed_cloud_url tripwire
was silently dead: tools/verify.sh mangled the regex backslashes, so the
pattern failed to compile and the gate falsely reported PASS.

- client.rs: delete authenticate_as_admin, its sole (impersonation)
  caller branch, and the ADMIN_API_TOKEN / USE_WEB_LOGIN env handles it
  needed. IMPERSONATE_LOGIN stays (still used by the kept auth paths).
  The removed early return had anchored the spawn closure's error type,
  so pin it explicitly with anyhow::Ok. Drop the now-unused Request /
  AsyncReadExt imports and the dead `this` binding.
- http_client.rs: delete the orphaned build_zed_api_url,
  build_zed_cloud_url and build_zed_cloud_url_with_query builders (the
  impersonation call was their last referrer) and the unused
  serde::Serialize import.
- client.rs actions!: drop the orphaned client::SignIn action. Patch
  0037 removed its handler but left the declaration -- a
  palette-dispatchable "Sign in to Zed account" command that did
  nothing.
- docs/authentication.md: de-macro the now-dangling {#action
  client::SignIn} reference so the docs action manifest stays valid.
- client.rs tests: import settings::SettingsContent. Pre-existing latent
  breakage that kept the client test build from compiling; surfaced by
  --tests while validating this change.

cargo check -p client -p http_client -p cloud_api_client --tests is clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
